Alcázar is the ninth planet from the star Aurelius, orbiting in the outer reaches of the system beyond the violet giant [[Amatista]]. It is the largest and most massive planet in the Aurelius system, possessing a mass equivalent to 510 times that of [[Adonia]]. It is a gas giant of immense proportions, often referred to as the King of the Outer Dark.

The most defining feature of Alcázar is its extreme axial tilt of approximately 98 degrees. Unlike the other planets which rotate relatively upright in their orbits, Alcázar rolls on its side. This unique orientation means its poles face the star alternately for decades at a time, resulting in extreme seasonal insolation cycles that drive complex atmospheric dynamics.

Visually, Alcázar presents a serene yet imposing facade. Its atmosphere is colored in muted tones of butterscotch, pale yellow, and soft cream, created by high-altitude haze layers of hydrocarbon smog. Due to its tilt, the atmospheric bands appear to run vertically or diagonally across the disk when viewed from the ecliptic plane of the inner system, giving it the nickname The Slanted World.

==Physical characteristics==
===Atmosphere===
The atmosphere of Alcázar is deep and relatively calm compared to the turbulent [[Quetzal]] or [[Amatista]]. The primary constituents are hydrogen and helium, but the lower temperatures at this distance allow for the condensation of ammonia and methane clouds, which are obscured by a thick upper layer of photochemical haze.

Despite its calm appearance, the planet possesses massive, slow-moving cyclonic systems. The "Cream Bands" are vast jet streams that circle the planet. Because of the extreme tilt, the Coriolis forces act differently here, creating weather patterns that spiral from the equator toward the poles in long, languid curves.

===Internal structure===
Alcázar is believed to have a massive rocky core, perhaps 20 to 30 times the mass of [[Adonia]], surrounded by a mantle of water, ammonia, and methane ices. Above this is a thick layer of metallic hydrogen, similar to Quetzal but cooler and denser. The immense gravity of the planet has allowed it to capture and hold a retinue of over 80 moons, creating a miniature solar system of its own.

==Orbit and rotation==
Alcázar orbits Aurelius at a distance of 11.20 AU, completing a revolution every 14,200 standard days (approx. 39 Adonian years). This slow orbit makes it a generational marker in Adonian culture; a human life is often measured by how many times Alcázar has returned to its natal position.

The planet rotates on its side once every 16.8 hours. This rolling motion means that for half of its orbit, one pole is bathed in continuous sunlight while the other is plunged into decades of darkness. This results in strange magnetospheric interactions, as the planet's magnetic field—which is offset from its rotational axis—wobbles wildly as it interacts with the solar wind, creating a "corkscrew" magnetotail.

==Name and etymology==
The name Alcázar comes from the Insulonian word for a fortress or palace. The name was chosen by early astronomers who viewed the planet's massive size and slow, deliberate movement as a symbol of an impregnable castle guarding the outer system.

In Sanese astronomical nomenclature, the planet is known as Shatensei (斜天星 [Shatensei]), translating to the Slanted Heaven Star or Tilted Sky Star. This name directly references the planet's unusual axial tilt, which was calculated long before spaceflight confirmed the visual diagonal banding.

